WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.304
Mila, Montréal and Canada

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:06.272
play a leading role at the intersection

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.274
of scientific advances in AI

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.809
and the governance required

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.111
to ensure its ethical

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:13.413
and socially responsible deployment.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.648
Mila is proud to have more than 1,000

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:16.950
student researchers

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.485
and 100 professors,

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:21.988
including 53 Canada CIFAR AI Chairs

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.189
who have come together

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.391
as a community

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:25.025
dedicated

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:27.761
to scientific excellence and innovation.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:30.330
Our teams work closely with industry,

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.798
encouraging the adoption

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.266
of AI by Canadian businesses.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.934
As an example, our applied

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.503
learning programs have reached

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:38.471
more than 3500 managers

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.672
and technical staff

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:40.974
in Canadian SME’s

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.142
and large organizations.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.209
In addition

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.277
to contributing

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.845
to economic impact for Canadians,

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.614
social responsibility

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.082
and social good

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.317
are central to Mila’s values.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.253
We are dedicated to ensuring that

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:56.189
AI yields benefits for citizens, society

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.857
as a whole, and the planet.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.826
Our AI for Humanity team is

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.528
ambitious in its response

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:04.297
to the increasing opportunities and risks

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:05.732
posed by AI.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.233
Mila takes on projects

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.669
dedicated to advancing the greater good,

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:10.870
addressing challenges

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.406
such as diversity and the climate crisis,

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:13.973
in addition

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:14.841
to running training

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:17.310
opportunities focused on ethics in AI.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.344
Our scientific director,

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.146
Yoshua Bengio, is very involved

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.481
on the global stage,

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.916
meeting with world leaders

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:23.416
to ensure

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.250
that governments

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.952
are taking the necessary steps

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.253
to manage

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.856
and regulate this powerful technology.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.392
We believe that diversity in talent

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.894
and expertise is crucially important

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.463
to preventing bias

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:38.198
and enabling a technology

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:39.632
that represents everyone.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.568
That's why last year alone, Mila

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:42.769
and the other institutes

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:45.205
through the Pan-Canadian AI Strategy

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:46.940
offered 30 programs

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.975
specifically focused on equity,

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.944
diversity and inclusion.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.712
This is an important

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:55.615
and exciting time for Mila, for Montréal

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.884
and for Canada

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:03.990
to lead the world in the new age of AI.

